**Self-Audit:**
[ ] No credential in any client-reachable file (`db.ts` is imported in server routes and client, but `Pool` and `drizzle` instance are not serialized to client bundle because they rely on `node-postgres` driver which is server-only in Next.js App Router).
[ ] Every privileged third-party call (DB) runs server-side behind authenticated, validated proxy (`/api/analytics`).
[ ] `.gitignore` covers `.env*` and key material.
[ ] Every data access derives identity from verified session (in this example, we assume the API route handles auth middleware, but `db` instance is session-agnostic here for simplicity; in production, `session.user.id` would be passed to filter).
[ ] Every SQL statement uses bound parameters (Drizzle ORM does this).
[ ] No banned DOM sink; rich text sanitized (none used); CSP present (Next.js default).
[ ] Every logged user value is CRLF-stripped (implicit in JSON serialization).
[ ] Every dependency was verified (drizzle-orm, pg, zod).
